Summary:
Use The Dojo Remembers as reference: full kinetic pointillist epic, no static shots, <2s cuts, heavy particle physics, aggressive camera, loud industrial-orchestral rhythm, constant motion and combat from frame one.”

REFERENCE STYLE: FULL KINETIC POINTILLIST EPIC
Use this video as the gold standard for everything that follows.

[Core Intent]
Mythic boss intro energy, not atmosphere
Impact in the first 0.5–1.0s
Designed to overwhelm immediately and never let go

[Pace & Structure]
Total length ~25s
EVERY shot < 2 seconds
No buildup, no calm, no meditation
Escalation is constant — energy never plateaus

[Motion Rules]
NO static shots, ever
Protagonist is always moving (running, dodging, striking, repositioning)
Camera is aggressive and physical: whip-pans, plunges, orbits, chase cams
Environment reacts violently to motion

[Physics & Texture]
Pointillist particles behave as heavy solid matter (sand + steel), never smoke
Every impact displaces mass (shockwaves, debris, compression)
Nothing floats unless actively forced
Air bends, pressure waves are visible

[Combat Language]
Attacks are staggered, chaotic, hostile
Multi-directional threats, near-misses, deflections
No hero poses — dominance comes from motion
Feels like a hunt or execution attempt, not a ritual

[Visual Style]
Extreme black & white contrast
Dense stippling / dots as structural material
Strong silhouettes, readable at any speed
Cinematic framing (2.39:1), violent scale shifts

[Audio & Rhythm]
Epic hybrid orchestral + industrial percussion

135–150 BPM
Constant sub-bass pressure synced to impacts
Loud, aggressive, theatrical mix
Metallic shrieks, air tearing, debris shear
Overall Feeling
Relentless
Violent
Mythic
Overstimulating in a good way
Audience should feel attacked, not invited

